      "_id": "69ec05123a63baf2053a00d9",
      "latePostId": "69e9decdc03088bf3dec650a",
      "content": "After decades of stagnation, nuclear power is being revived — not by climate legislation, but by AI electricity demand 🤖⚡\n\nAI + Nuclear: The Full Story\n\nThe electricity problem:\n→ US electricity demand was flat for 20 years\n→ AI model training: single frontier model = tens of millions of kWh\n→ AI inference: continuous massive baseload demand 24/7/365\n→ DOE projection: +15% US electricity demand by 2028\n→ Primary driver: AI data centers\n→ The grid was not built for this\n\nWhy nuclear specifically:\n→ AI data centers need: firm, dispatchable, 24/7, carbon-free power\n→ Solar/wind: variable, weather-dependent\n→ Batteries: bridge hours, not weeks\n→ Natural gas: dispatchable but carbon-emitting\n→ Nuclear: 92% capacity factor, continuous, zero-carbon, weather-independent\n→ Perfect match for data center load profiles\n\nThe deals signed:\n\nMicrosoft × Three Mile Island:\n→ 20-year power purchase agreement (September 2024)\n→ TMI Unit 1 shut in 2019 for economic reasons\n→ Restarting in 2028 specifically for Microsoft AI infrastructure\n\nGoogle × Kairos Power:\n→ SMR contract, first delivery targeted 2030\n→ Additional SMRs through 2035\n\nAmazon × X-energy:\n→ Investment and energy offtake for SMR deployment\n\nOracle:\n→ Planning nuclear-powered data center campuses\n\nSmall modular reactors (SMRs):\n→ Traditional nuclear: 10+ year permit and build timeline\n→ SMRs: factory-manufactured, faster deployment, smaller footprint\n→ Can site closer to data centers (shorter transmission)\n→ Active developers: Kairos, TerraPower, NuScale, X-energy\n\nThe irony:\n→ 30 years of climate policy couldn't restart US nuclear construction at scale\n→ The electricity demand of language models may accomplish it in 5 years\n\n#aifacts #nuclear #energypolicy #datacenters #aiindustry #artificialintelligence #cleanenergy #smr #techenergy #climatetech",
