      "content": "AI solved a 50-year biology Grand Challenge — then gave the answer to the entire world for free 🤖🧬\n\nAlphaFold2: What Actually Happened\n\nThe problem:\n→ Protein function = determined by 3D shape\n→ Shape = determined by amino acid sequence\n→ Predicting 3D shape from sequence = protein folding problem\n→ Worked on since 1972 by thousands of researchers globally\n→ A 100-amino acid protein has an astronomically large conformational space\n→ Brute-force computation: physically impossible\n\nBefore AlphaFold (as of 2020):\n→ Experimental methods: X-ray crystallography, cryo-EM\n→ Each structure: months to years of lab work, $100K-$1M+\n→ Protein Data Bank total structures in 50 years: ~180,000\n\nAlphaFold2 at CASP14 (2020):\n→ Predicted structures with accuracy matching experimental methods\n→ Previous best AI: ~40% accuracy\n→ AlphaFold2: ~90%+ accuracy across diverse protein families\n→ Competition organizers: 'a solution to the problem'\n\nWhat DeepMind did next:\n→ Released source code as open source\n→ Released predicted structures for entire human proteome: free\n→ Expanded to all proteins in 48 model organisms: free\n→ Expanded to 200M+ structures covering nearly all known protein sequences: free\n→ Researchers who spent careers on one protein found it solved overnight\n\nThe impact:\n→ 'Undruggable' proteins became targetable\n→ Drug discovery timelines compressed by years\n→ Malaria, neglected diseases, antibiotic resistance: all advanced\n→ 2M+ researchers actively using the database\n\n2024 Nobel Prize in Chemistry:\n→ Demis Hassabis (DeepMind CEO) + John Jumper (lead researcher)\n→ Most consequential AI medical application in history\n→ Given away for free\n\n#aifacts #alphafold #proteinfolding #deepmind #aibreakthrough #artificialintelligence #biology #drugdiscovery #nobelprize #scienceai",
